  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi Donor Trust Fund for the Global Program on Fisheries (PROFISH)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Overall goal is to strengthen governance of the world&apos;s fisheries. Based on the Bank&apos;s Approach Paper, &apos;Saving Fish a nd Fishers&apos; the strengthened governance is aimed at improving sustainable livelihoods in coastal and fishing communities and making concrete progress towards meeting the WSSD objectives and specific fisheries targets of the WSSD Plan of Implementation (e.g. restoring the health of fish stocks by 2015).
 
 Country-level objectives are (a) to prepare policy analyses to build national consensus on paths to effective sector governance andreform; (b) to align donor interventions; and (c) to build capacity for reform and sustainable fishery management.
 
 Global and regional goods objectives: (a) to build global and regional awareness and consensus on reforms; and (b) to improved fisheries management tools.
 
 This TF is being established partly to overcome an accounting difficulty with TF 054432, namely the inability of DFID to contributeto aTF with a retroactive financing clause. The scope of the TF activities reflects the decisions of the PROFISH Steering Committeeover the past 2 years. This TF would also be used to support project preparation studies, sustainable aquaculture and freshwater fisheries and secondments (special assisgnments).The governance arrangements for this TF are identical to TF 054432 (see 41 below).&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
